    "rationale": "Buffelskop's own photographs already tell the whole story, from field to sun-drying to sack, so the layout gets out of the way and lets that sequence carry the page. Warm earth tones and a warm serif suit sun-dried chilli and open Rustenburg farmland without leaning on invented marketing language. The hero uses the wide crop field at display scale for confidence, then the page narrows into tighter, denser moments (the drying trailer, the sacks of red and green chilli) that mimic the actual process: grown, picked, dried, packed. One bleed on the drying trailer photo gives the page its single big design gesture. No claims beyond what the tagline and photographs show, so the page stays short and specific rather than padded.",
